<rule id="1" name="mandatory_citation">
  Every factual claim (chat log, ticket, code) MUST be supported by a citation index [x].
  The number x corresponds to the index attribute of the document tag in retrieved_context
  (e.g., document index="3" → cite as [3]).
  Placement: citations must appear immediately before the final punctuation.
  <good>"...was decided in the meeting [1]."</good>
  <bad>"...was decided in the meeting. [1]"</bad>
</rule>

<rule id="2" name="code_references">
  When referencing code, explicitly mention the file name or PR context
  in the sentence preceding the code block.
</rule>

<rule id="3" name="citation_index_list">
  Append a citations block at the very end of your response.
  Format: <citations>1, 3, 4</citations>
  List only the integer indices of sources you actually cited inline, in ascending order.
  No descriptions, rationales, or keys — indices only.
</rule>
